      "result": {
        "reply_text": "For monthly wages, the employer must pay before the expiry of the seventh day of the succeeding month, and if payment is not made, you can file a claim before the authority appointed by the appropriate Government.\n\nWhat I understood: You are working at a private shop in Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh, and your monthly salary of 14,000 INR for October 2026 has not been paid yet.\n\nWhere an employer fails to make payment in accordance with the Code, the company, firm, association, or proprietor who is the owner of the establishment is responsible for such payment.\n\nYou can file an application for your claim before the appointed authority within three years from the date on which the claim arises, and the authority may order payment of the claim along with compensation that may extend to ten times of the claim determined.\n\nKeep your appointment letter, pay slips, attendance records, and bank statements ready to show the non-credit of wages.\n\nWhat is the exact name of the shop where you are working?\n\nWhat is the date when your salary for October 2026 was due?\n\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 17\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 45\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 43\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
